WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.000
You're in the middle of something that matters to you,

00:03.500 --> 00:08.000
something you've been building towards across this whole experience.

00:08.800 --> 00:11.200
The plan just changed.

00:11.900 --> 00:13.800
You don't have the full picture just yet,

00:14.500 --> 00:17.300
but the last thing you tried didn't work.

00:17.900 --> 00:21.600
A person you trust strongly disagrees with your call,

00:21.600 --> 00:25.400
and you already have more on your plate than you know what to do with.

00:25.900 --> 00:29.400
And people are watching how you handle this.

00:30.000 --> 00:33.400
Before you rush to respond to any of it,

00:34.000 --> 00:36.600
what do you notice right now?

00:47.100 --> 00:51.000
This is what makes the real moments different.

00:51.000 --> 00:54.800
Pressure rarely arrives one variable at a time.

00:55.000 --> 01:00.600
For five lessons, you've practiced these pressures one at a time.

01:01.000 --> 01:05.100
Now they're happening together. Which one is pulling hardest on you?

01:05.200 --> 01:06.800
It's not a verdict.

01:06.900 --> 01:13.300
It's the exact information, the data, this whole experience was built to surface.

01:14.000 --> 01:15.300
What do you think first?

01:15.900 --> 01:16.800
How do you feel?

01:17.400 --> 01:18.500
What do you decide?

01:19.200 --> 01:24.600
How do you access your best decision in the moment of pressure and change?

01:36.600 --> 01:39.500
While you're still responding,

01:39.500 --> 01:42.700
one more piece of information changes things yet again.

01:49.100 --> 01:53.900
Six lessons ago, we asked you to notice your first response.

01:54.700 --> 01:59.700
Since then, you've practiced changing plans, moving with uncertainty,

02:00.000 --> 02:04.800
recovering after a miss, and staying open in disagreements.

02:05.340 --> 02:10.040
That's the difference between knowing what good leadership looks like

02:10.040 --> 02:14.740
and being able to access it when the conditions get hard.

02:15.340 --> 02:17.740
You've practiced the latter.
